  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nModels have been consistent with showing the broad upper-level ridge \nretrograding to the west over much of the southern CONUS this \nweekend and becoming dominant through the middle part of next week. \nThis feature will continue to yield above normal temperatures each \nday, with afternoon highs in the upper 90s for most. Though spots \nalong the Pecos River and Rio Grande Valleys can expect to see \nmaximum temperatures above the century mark. Cooler tempertures in \nthe upper 80s to low 90s can be found in the mountains. Moist \nsoutheasterly upslope flow and maybe some minor disturbances in the \nflow aloft could bring isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms across the western higher terrain each afternoon \nthrough at least Sunday. After Sunday, shower and storm chances \nbecome less likely, but not completely out of question. Otherwise, \nthe remainder of the area remains dry through the extended as \nsinking motion under the ridge inhibits convective initiation. Low \ntempertures continue to range in the 60s in the mountains and 70s \nelsewhere.\n  \nGreening",
